spans.s:
Cakravartin,
(1) n. of one of the Uṣṇīṣa-rājānaḥ (see uṣṇīṣa 3): Mmk 〔41.10〕;
(2) n. of one of the krodha, q.v.: Dharmas 〔11〕.

cakrika, adj., or subst. m.,
(1) some sort of prefessional entertainer, perh. a juggler who does tricks with wheels or discs (cf. BR s.v. cakrin, 7; a Skt. Lex. possibly gives this mg., but it is uncertain): Mv 〔iii.113.2〕 (mss. here corrupt); 〔442.8〕;
(2) (a) tricky, crafty (person): ˚kaḥ Mvy 〔7326〕; this seems to be the mg. indicated by Tib. (five renderings), Chin., and Jap., and supported by the adjoining words (jihma, kuṭila, Mvy 〔7324—5〕); cf. Skt. (Rājat.) cakrikā, Ränke (BR);
(3) see s.v. cākrika.
